        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0071214"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any process that results in a change in state or activity of a cell (in terms of movement, secretion, enzyme production, gene expression, etc.) as a result of an electromagnetic radiation stimulus. Electromagnetic radiation is a propagating wave in space with electric and magnetic components. These components oscillate at right angles to each other and to the direction of propagation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>mah</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2009-12-18T01:59:37Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>cellular response to electromagnetic radiation stimulus</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
