            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The outermost layer of a blood vessel, composed mainly of fibrous tissue.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>TODO - note terminological problems. WP says tunica external layer of blood vessel. FMA says tunica externa = adventitia, and is FMA adventitia covers other kinds of vessels. Here we opt for a lengthier name that attempts to disambiguate. There is no precise FMA equivalent, as FMA has tunica externa of arteries, veins, genital ducts etc as siblings</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>The outermost layer of a blood vessel, surrounding the tunica media. It is mainly composed of collagen. The collagen serves to anchor the blood vessel to nearby organs, giving it stability[Wikipedia:Tunica_externa_(vessels)].</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunica_externa_(vessels)"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://linkedlifedata.com/resource/umls/id/C0225342"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/61066005"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0002010</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:36299</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C33818</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
